		{"id":"4300e65803164afd","type":"group","label":"NAVIGATION","x":-1050,"y":-380,"width":2600,"height":210,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"e631a64b67414eac","type":"file","file":"CERNAL Architecture.canvas","x":-950,"y":-330,"width":360,"height":100,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"c211e21803344c48","type":"file","file":"Maps/05 Platform Domain and Database.canvas","x":-500,"y":-330,"width":430,"height":100,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"5532738c78844335","type":"file","file":"Maps/13 Engine Job State Machine.canvas","x":-20,"y":-330,"width":430,"height":100,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"68e0a89f43494b21","type":"file","file":"Maps/15 Storage and Artifact Flow.canvas","x":460,"y":-330,"width":430,"height":100,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"ea30cd59a12241b6","type":"file","file":"Maps/08 Platform-Engine API Contract.canvas","x":940,"y":-330,"width":430,"height":100,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"4208fed9a415480d","type":"group","label":"RELIABILITY · REPRODUCIBILITY · OBSERVABILITY","x":-1050,"y":-20,"width":2850,"height":1700,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"0ab66d6cb358446b","type":"text","text":"# Required identifiers\nAcross logs and records:\n- `workspace_id`\n- `project_id`\n- `analysis_run_id`\n- `engine_job_id`\n- `correlation_id`\n- `provider_job_id` (Engine-private)\n- artifact IDs / checksums\n\nA correlation ID should bridge Platform and Engine logs.","x":-900,"y":80,"width":520,"height":390,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"9635a251177c48a1","type":"text","text":"# Reproducibility Manifest\nRecord:\n- immutable input checksum/reference\n- normalized parameter snapshot\n- organism/base/target state\n- gate constraints\n- random seed / deterministic mode\n- Engine semantic version\n- scientific pipeline version\n- scoring profile/version\n- source commit\n- external tool versions\n- database/index versions\n- compute environment\n- timestamps/warnings\n- final artifact checksums","x":-250,"y":80,"width":620,"height":590,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"f34b4a200fb24c02","type":"text","text":"# Structured Logs\nPlatform and Engine log structured events with run/job/correlation IDs.\n\nSeparate:\n- user-safe error message\n- operator diagnostic detail\n- restricted stack trace / command output\n\nDo not leak secrets or private paths.","x":500,"y":80,"width":520,"height":390,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"cc888419933b486f","type":"text","text":"# Operational Metrics\nTrack:\n- submissions/day\n- queue wait\n- execution duration\n- failures by stage\n- retries\n- cancellation latency\n- result import lag\n- artifact sizes\n- storage usage\n- stuck-job age\n- API auth failures","x":1120,"y":80,"width":500,"height":410,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"c33c6c9d6d814ffe","type":"text","text":"# Retry model\n**Safe to retry**\n- Platform worker tasks\n- Engine status polling\n- result-manifest fetch/import\n- idempotent job submission\n\n**Do not blindly retry**\nScientific computation after a terminal failure without a policy, because it can consume resources or obscure reproducibility. Prefer explicit new run/retry semantics.","x":-900,"y":760,"width":600,"height":430,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"115c012ee9654eaa","type":"text","text":"# Health / Version\nPlatform:\n- health\n- build version\n- dependency health as appropriate\n\nEngine:\n- health\n- API version\n- Engine version\n- scientific capabilities\n\nAvoid exposing sensitive topology.","x":-170,"y":790,"width":500,"height":350,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"e5f28f79d606416e","type":"text","text":"# Suggested alerts\n- repeated Engine authentication failures\n- jobs stuck beyond expected stage duration\n- provider submission failures\n- storage exhaustion\n- result import failures\n- backup failures\n- unusual failure-rate spike","x":450,"y":790,"width":500,"height":350,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"ef3bdf2c02314590","type":"text","text":"# Backups & retention\nPlatform:\n- PostgreSQL backups\n- durable object/file storage\n- restore testing\n\nEngine:\n- temporary workspace retention policy\n- keep enough execution metadata for diagnosis\n- do not use Engine workspace as the only durable product result store","x":1080,"y":790,"width":550,"height":390,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"c49ac15a526540c4","type":"text","text":"## Design principle\nA job is not reproducible because “the same button can be clicked again.” It is reproducible when the system can identify the exact data, parameters, versions, tools, seed and outputs that defined the original computation.","x":-900,"y":1320,"width":2500,"height":240,"color":"4"}
	],
	"edges":[]
}